  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Adjusting the Real User Height is a simple way to make operating some avatars feel more comfortable, and more 1:1 to physical movements. At times, that means we have to go from the maximum height to the minimum height and vice versa. Currently, the quickest way to jump between widely varied heights is to rapidly click the up/down buttons in the setting until we get there. It can get tedious pretty quickly. \nI figure the simplest QoL addition would be to allow us to hold the up/down buttons in the setting so it can raise/lower the height repeatedly over time, at a fairly quick rate. This alone would help a bunch. (Just so the menu moving isn't too much an issue, maybe have it so the height only changes after you release either arrow button for a second or so.)\nAs an alternative thought, there could be a button below the setting that allows us to save the User Height to the active avatar locally, if possible. But also, have a button that saves the default height you'd like to be set to when you load an avatar without a personally set User Height. Not as simple, but it's a bit more automated when set up.",
